Z||000000||Majik||06-20-2000||03:27 PM||||Okay, need a bit of help here.  I live in New Mexico, and we don't have the privalage of having a Fiero car club.  So a friend and I are wanting to start one up.  I am currently working on the web page, and should have something soft up by this weekend with a couple of pictures.<P>I've read a lot of information about car clubs off of the other car club home pages, and want to know what all your car club does, and maybe even how you started your car club!  What kind of information and techniques do you use to draw in members (there are quite a few Fiero's that drive around Albuquerque).  <P>I've been jealous of all of the pictures showing the 20 Fiero's lined up and someone in the background eating a hotdog (you know who you are!)...and have wanted to get something like that going for a while.  Any information that you have will be greatly appreciated!  <P>I am working on a local Pontiac dealership for sponsorship/meeting place/discounts/etc.  Thank you in advance for your help!<P>Todd Van Sant<BR>86 Red/Grey GT<BR>Future President of New Mexico Fiero Association<P>(I'll post the url to our home when it is up and running)||||reg||3
Z||000001||tgowens||06-20-2000||03:34 PM||||Hi Todd - take a look at our club site I designed and see if that helps any....... <A HREF="http://www.goldengatefieros.org" TARGET=_blank>www.goldengatefieros.org</A>  and maybe look at the photos of the recent poker run we held two weeks ago....the photos are on the 'gallery' page......||||reg||1
